<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  CALL OF VALOR's three abilities.

  UNLIKE EVERY OTHER SHOUT IN THIS MOD, THIS ONE TARGETS A CELL. The others send a cone, a lane
  or a ring out from the caster; this opens a portal where the player points, and the hero walks
  out of it. So targetParams allows LOCATIONS and nothing else - no pawns, no buildings - and
  targetRequired is true, which is the opposite of every self-cast shout here.

  There is deliberately NO <cooldownTicksRange>. Only Dragon Aspect needs vanilla's per-ability
  cooldown, because it is a once-per-day power; this is a quest reward governed by its Thu'um
  cost and the shared shout lockout, both in the ShoutDef.

  ALL THREE ARE IDENTICAL, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. The user, 2026-08-01: *"ALL three words are
  learned at the same time during a quest... So no need to actualy tinker on what one word or
  two words will."* He is never at one or two words, so a ladder across them describes states
  that cannot happen. An earlier version scaled range, stay and cost across the three; it was
  removed rather than left to mislead whoever tunes this next.

  The three defs remain because the shout system is one ability per word. Whichever the level
  resolves to, the hero arrives at full strength.

  RANGE IS SHORT - 5.9, a few tiles - because the user asked for the summoning to land close to
  the Dovahkiin. He is a bodyguard stepping in beside her, not artillery placed across the map.
  Line of sight IS required: he steps out of a hole in the world, and opening one through a wall
  reads as a bug even when it is not.

  HIS OWN ICON, generated 2026-08-01 to the user's spec: bright white at the head running down to
  grey at the tip, with the head's core circle in the summon's own blue. That blue is C_AZURE
  read from Tools/ValorPalette.ps1 - the same file his armour and his greatsword read - so the
  icon quotes the hero rather than a blue that merely looks like his. It briefly borrowed Dragon
  Aspect's icon; that is over. Regenerating proved the other 15 icons byte-identical.
-->
<Defs>

  <AbilityDef Name="Dovahkiin_CallOfValorBase" Abstract="True">
    <hostile>false</hostile>
    <targetRequired>true</targetRequired>
    <showWhenDrafted>true</showWhenDrafted>
    <displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>true</displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>
    <disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>false</disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>
    <iconPath>UI/Abilities/Dovahkiin_Shout_CallOfValor</iconPath>
    <verbProperties>
      <verbClass>Verb_CastAbility</verbClass>
      <warmupTime>1.4</warmupTime>
      <drawAimPie>false</drawAimPie>
      <requireLineOfSight>true</requireLineOfSight>
      <targetParams>
        <canTargetLocations>true</canTargetLocations>
        <canTargetPawns>false</canTargetPawns>
        <canTargetBuildings>false</canTargetBuildings>
        <canTargetItems>false</canTargetItems>
        <canTargetSelf>false</canTargetSelf>
      </targetParams>
    </verbProperties>
  </AbilityDef>

  <!-- ===================== Hun - one word ===================== -->
  <AbilityDef ParentName="Dovahkiin_CallOfValorBase">
    <defName>Dovahkiin_Ability_CallOfValor_1</defName>
    <label>hun</label>
    <description>Hero, Champion, Legend. A legend of the old world steps out of Sovngarde, greatsword in hand, and stands with you until the echo fades.</description>
    <verbProperties>
      <verbClass>Verb_CastAbility</verbClass>
      <range>5.9</range>
      <warmupTime>1.4</warmupTime>
      <drawAimPie>false</drawAimPie>
      <requireLineOfSight>true</requireLineOfSight>
      <targetParams>
        <canTargetLocations>true</canTargetLocations>
        <canTargetPawns>false</canTargetPawns>
        <canTargetBuildings>false</canTargetBuildings>
        <canTargetItems>false</canTargetItems>
        <canTargetSelf>false</canTargetSelf>
      </targetParams>
    </verbProperties>
    <comps>
      <li Class="Dovahkiin.CompProperties_Shout">
        <shout>Dovahkiin_Shout_CallOfValor</shout>
        <level>1</level>
      </li>
      <li Class="Dovahkiin.CompProperties_CallOfValor">
        <level>1</level>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_AbilityRequiresCapacity">
        <capacity>Talking</capacity>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </AbilityDef>

